From 666bf5e6a99ae2a470c738fc74ba4cfd73773aed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:18:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-103: a double-click on a property's name goes to
 its value in the HTML, selected (0.103.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "先讓使用者可以和 wpf 改 code 一樣方便有效率". In WPF's split view the
XAML of the element is right there; here, from a property in the grid, the value
had to be looked for in the HTML by hand. Now a double-click on a property's
name opens the page's HTML beside the designer with that value selected, ready
to be typed over: htmledit.propRange(text, id, prop) -- Left / Top / Width /
Height / AutoSize / Font.* / Color / Alignment / Visible = the style
declaration's value (Left of an input on its positioning <span>, a panel's font
and alignment on its caption <span class="pnlCap">), Caption / Text = the
caption text (an input's value attribute), Enabled = disabled, Alias = title;
not written = the element's tag (as HTML 原始碼 does).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 187, panels, real VS Code 159): lib
(propRange, 11 cases); smoke (Left -> "54px", Caption -> "Save", Font.Name ->
the element); panels (a double-click on Top posts revealProp; its tooltip says
so).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
